<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n48739" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θηρῐ-ᾰκός</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ή</span>,
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">όν</span>, (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θηρίον</span>)
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>concerning venomous
			beasts</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λόγος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Dsc.
					<u>Ther.Praef.</u>
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Φιλῖνοσ&lt;ὁ&gt;
			θ</span>., the writer on this subject, <i><span class="en">
				Philum.
				<u>Ven.</u>
				6.1
			</span></i>: <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἡ -κή</span> (sc. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀντίδοτος</span>) and antidote <i>against a
				poisonous bite</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Androm.
			</span></i> ap.<i><span class="en">
				Gal.
				14.32
			</span></i>, etc.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θ. φάρμακα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					17(2).337
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θηριακά</span>, title of
			Nicander's poem on such antidotes; of other works, <i><span class="en">
				Gal.
				14.7
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θ. ἄμπελος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>Gp.</u>
					4.8.1
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Plin.
				<u>HN</u>
				14.117
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θ. [οἶνος</span>] <i><span class="en">
				Dsc.
				5.53
			</span></i>.</div>
